{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Executive summary{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<h1>VPN Security Assessment - Executive Summary</h1>
<p class="muted">Capture: <b>{{ a.filename }}</b> &nbsp;|&nbsp; Generated: {{ generated }}</p>

<table style="margin-top:8pt;">
  <tr>
    <td style="width:34%; padding:0; border:none;">
      <table>
        <tr><td class="risk" style="background-color:{{ risk_color }};">{{ a.risk_level }} RISK</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="risk-sub" style="background-color:{{ risk_color }};">
          {% if a.score is not none %}Security score {{ a.score }} / 100{% else %}No score could be calculated{% endif %}
        </td></tr>
      </table>
    </td>
    <td style="width:66%; border:none; padding-left:12pt;">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">In one sentence</h3>
      <p>
      {% if a.score is none %}
        This capture does not reveal how the VPN was configured, so its security cannot be rated from the traffic alone.
      {% elif a.assessment.score_capped and a.raw_score is not none and a.raw_score >= 80 %}
        The settings that could be checked are strong, but too little could be established from this capture to call the VPN low-risk.
      {% elif a.risk_level == "LOW" %}
        The VPN uses strong settings for everything that could be checked.
      {% elif a.risk_level == "MEDIUM" %}
        The VPN is reasonably protected, but some settings should be improved.
      {% else %}
        The VPN uses settings that are weak by modern standards and should be changed.
      {% endif %}
      {% if a.traffic %}The encrypted traffic looks like <b>{{ a.traffic.label|lower }}</b>.{% endif %}
      </p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<div class="notice" style="border-color:#2b7bb9; background-color:#eef5fb;">
  <b>Assessment completeness: {{ a.assessment.completeness_pct|round|int }}%.</b>
  Only this share of the security facts that matter could be established from the capture.
  {% if a.assessment.score_capped %}The score is therefore <b>capped at {{ a.assessment.score_cap }}</b>; the facts that are known would alone give {{ a.raw_score }}.{% endif %}
  {% if a.assessment.unknown_facts %}Not determinable: {{ a.assessment.unknown_facts|join(", ") }}.{% endif %}
</div>
{% if a.score_basis in ["declared", "mixed"] %}
<div class="notice">
  <b>Important:</b> {% if a.score_basis == "declared" %}the settings below come from the VPN configuration named in the capture's file name (declared by the test setup), not from the traffic itself,{% else %}some of the settings below come from the capture's file name rather than the traffic itself,{% endif %}
  because the readable part of the VPN negotiation is not in this capture. Treat the rating as "what was configured", not "what was measured".
</div>
{% endif %}
{% if a.errors %}<div class="error"><b>Part of the analysis failed:</b> {{ a.errors|join(" ") }}</div>{% endif %}

<h2>Security settings</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Setting</th><th>Value</th><th>Rating</th><th>Where the value comes from</th></tr>
  {% for b in a.breakdown %}
  <tr>
    <td><b>{{ b.factor }}</b></td>
    <td>{{ b.value }}</td>
    <td><span class="badge" style="background-color:{{ rating_color[b.rating] }};">{{ b.rating|upper }}</span></td>
    <td>{% if b.source == "observed" %}Read from the capture{% elif b.source == "inferred" %}Inferred from packet sizes{% elif b.source == "declared" %}Declared by file name{% else %}Not determinable{% endif %}</td>
  </tr>
  <tr><td colspan="4" class="muted" style="border-top:none;">{{ b.reason }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="muted">The score is a weighted average of the rated settings (cipher 40%, key exchange 40%, forward secrecy 20%).
Settings that cannot be determined are left out instead of being counted as weak. Mode is shown for information and is not scored.</p>

<h2>Recommended actions</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th style="width:12%;">Priority</th><th>Action</th></tr>
  {% for prio, text in recommendations %}
  <tr><td><b>{{ prio }}</b></td><td>{{ text }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>

{% if before_after %}
<div class="notice" style="border-color:#2b7bb9; background-color:#eef5fb;">
  <b>If the recommended configuration were applied (projection, not a measurement):</b>
  score now {{ before_after.before.score if before_after.before.score is not none else "n/a" }} ({{ before_after.before.risk_level }});
  from a new passive capture {{ before_after.after_passive_capture.score }} ({{ before_after.after_passive_capture.risk_level }});
  with the gateway configuration reviewed directly {{ before_after.after_config_review.score }} ({{ before_after.after_config_review.risk_level }}).
  <span class="muted">A capture alone cannot show forward secrecy or the authentication method, so it cannot reach 100.</span>
</div>
{% endif %}

{% if a.traffic %}
<h2>What is travelling through the tunnel</h2>
<p>Without decrypting anything, the size and timing pattern of the encrypted packets was matched against five known traffic types.
Best match: <b>{{ a.traffic.label }}</b> (model confidence {{ (a.traffic.confidence * 100)|round|int }}%).</p>
{% if a.anomalies %}
<h3>Unusual traffic flags</h3>
<ul>{% for x in a.anomalies %}<li><b>{{ x.severity }} - {{ x.name }}:</b> {{ x.description }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
{% else %}<p>No unusual traffic patterns were flagged.</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}

<h2>What this report cannot tell you</h2>
<ul>
  <li>An IPsec capture only shows the cipher and key-exchange group when the start of the VPN negotiation was captured. Whether forward secrecy is on is negotiated in an encrypted step and is not visible to an observer. Tunnel versus transport mode and the cipher family (CBC or GCM) can only be estimated statistically from packet sizes, and are marked "inferred" with a confidence.</li>
  <li>The traffic-type label is a statistical guess from packet sizes and timing, trained on five scripted traffic types. It is not proof of what users did.</li>
</ul>
{% endblock %}
